  "narrative": "With 606 deaths by February 2026, a continuation of a high front-loaded pace could push the total to exceed 1,000 by end-April, but monthly variability and reporting lags keep the outcome uncertain. The balance of supportive factors (pace and weather) against dampening ones (policy responses) yields a mid-range probability rather than a near-certainty.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.65,
      "basis": "reference_class is annual Mediterranean fatalities tracked by IOM Missing Migrants; anchor reflects a cautious starting point around mid-0.6 for a four-month outcome under high early-year activity"
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Pace carryover from February 2026 (606 by 28 Feb)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "If the February pace holds or accelerates into March–April, enough deaths could accumulate to surpass 1,000 by end-April."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Weather and crossing conditions in early 2026",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Unfavorable seas or persistent storms can sustain higher crossing fatality rates."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Reporting lags and data gaps in Missing Migrants",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Delays can mean later revisions raise the final tallies beyond observed pace."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Policy responses and SAR capacity",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Stronger search-and-rescue and policy changes could reduce crossings and fatalities, offsetting pace-driven risk."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Seasonal variability and March–April uncertainty",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Month-to-month volatility makes precise forecasting hard; information is uncertain."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Starting from a 0.65 anchor, I increased probability for pace and weather, modestly increased for data-lag risk, decreased for SAR/policy countermeasures, and kept a neutral note for seasonality. The resulting range reflects substantial uncertainty; the estimate is calibrated to be neither overly optimistic nor overly pessimistic given the mixed signals."
  }
}
